# Admin AI Guide

Use this guide when you want an AI helper to work on the admin area of Landly.

## What the AI should understand

The admin area manages:

- Dashboard overview
- Users management
- Seller approval
- Land listings moderation
- Reports and disputes
- Logout and sidebar navigation
- Modals, buttons, filters, and table actions

## IMPORTANT: Analyze the project first

**BEFORE asking the AI to make changes:**

The AI needs to understand the whole codebase structure so it doesn't break other parts.

Tell the AI to:

- Read the Dashboard_Admin.php file to see the current code
- Check the component structure (app/Views/Pages/Admin/Components/)
- Compare with Dashboard_Buyer.php and Dashboard_Seller.php to understand shared patterns
- Identify all section IDs (#dashboard-section, #users-section, etc.)
- Check the sidebar navigation structure and how data-section attributes work
- Understand the storage keys and state management (adminDashboardActiveSection)
- See what colors and styles are used (CSS variables like --green-900, --cream-100, --accent)
- Check the UserModel, MessageModel, and other Models to understand the data flow
- Look at existing Controllers to understand how data is passed to views
- Review the Config/ folder for settings that might affect the admin area
- Understand the difference between admin, buyer, and seller roles

**Why this matters:**

Each role (Admin, Buyer, Seller) has its own:

- Dashboard file (Dashboard_Admin.php, Dashboard_Buyer.php, Dashboard_Seller.php)
- Navigation structure
- Section components
- Data relationships (Users, Sellers, Listings, Reports models)

Changes to the admin area must NOT:

- Break the buyer or seller dashboard
- Modify shared Models or Controllers used by other roles
- Remove or rename existing section IDs that other code depends on
- Change the authentication or session logic
- Affect the router or filters that other roles use

## Best way to prompt the AI

When you ask the AI to do something, give it:

- The exact page or file
- The problem or task
- The section of the admin panel involved
- What the expected result should be
- Any design or behavior rules to follow

## Prompt Template

Use this format:

```text
You are working on the Landly admin dashboard.

FIRST: Analyze the codebase:
- Read c:\Users\ajcat\OneDrive\Desktop\Landly Website\landly\app\Views\Pages\Admin\Dashboard_Admin.php
